{"name":"Alibi","hex":"#d4cbc4","fetched":"2026-10-20","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"alibi","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The plea or mode of defense under which a person on trial for a crime proves or attempts to prove being in another place when the alleged act was committed.","An excuse, especially one used to avoid responsibility or blame."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To provide an alibi for.","To provide an excuse for."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alibi"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alibi","blocks":[{"text":"An alibi is a statement by a person under suspicion in a crime that they were in a different place when the offence was committed. During a police investigation, all suspects are usually asked to provide details of their whereabouts during the relevant time period, which, where possible, would usually be confirmed by other persons or in other ways."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alibi","wikidata":"Q468947"},{"title":"Alibi (Sevdaliza, Pabllo Vittar and Yseult song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Alibi\" is a song by Iranian-Dutch artist Sevdaliza, Brazilian singer Pabllo Vittar and French singer-songwriter Yseult. It was released on 28 June 2024 through Twisted Elegance as the second single from Sevdaliza's third studio album, Heroina. It samples Colombian musician Magín Díaz's song \"Rosa\", a version of the Cuban son \"Rosa, qué linda eres\", first recorded by the Sexteto Habanero Godínez in 1918. Musically, \"Alibi\" is an alternative pop song with club-influenced production that incorporates elements of various Latin genres, including funk carioca, reggaeton, and bullerengue."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/89/Sevdaliza%2C_Pabllo_Vittar_and_Yseult_-_Alibi.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alibi_(Sevdaliza%2C_Pabllo_Vittar_and_Yseult_song)","wikidata":"Q127414833"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikime